              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "If you are looking for the **iCloud Control Panel**, it has been renamed and is now officially called **iCloud for Windows**. \n\nBelow is a guide on how to download it for your PC, what it does, and how to manage your iCloud settings on other devices.\n\n---\n\n### 1. iCloud for Windows (formerly iCloud Control Panel)\nThis official app allows you to sync and manage your Apple data on a Windows PC.\n\n* **How to Download:**\n  * Open the **Microsoft Store** on your Windows PC and search for \"iCloud\".\n  * Alternatively, you can download it directly from [Apple Support](https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT204283).\n* **Key Features:**\n  * **iCloud Photos:** View, search, and download your iPhone photos directly in the Windows \"Photos\" app.\n  * **iCloud Drive:** Access and edit your files directly from Windows File Explorer.\n  * **iCloud Passwords:** Autofill, save, and manage your saved iCloud Keychain credentials using browser extensions for Chrome, Edge, or Firefox.\n  * **Contacts, Calendars, & Bookmarks:** Sync your iOS contacts and calendars with Outlook, and sync your Safari bookmarks with your Windows browsers.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Access iCloud Settings on Apple Devices\nIf you wanted to find the iCloud \"control panel\" or settings menu on your Apple devices:\n\n* **On iPhone, iPad, or Apple Vision Pro:**\n  1. Open the **Settings** app.\n  2. Tap **[Your Name]** at the top.\n  3. Tap **iCloud** to manage your storage, apps using iCloud, device backups, and more.\n\n* **On Mac (macOS Ventura or later):**\n  1. Click the **Apple logo (\uf8ff)** in the top-left corner.\n  2. Go to **System Settings**.\n  3. Click **[Your Name]** at the top of the sidebar, then select **iCloud**.\n\n* **On Mac (macOS Monterey or earlier):**\n  1. Click the **Apple logo (\uf8ff)** and go to **System Preferences**.\n  2. Click **Apple ID**, then select **iCloud** from the sidebar.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Managing iCloud from a Web Browser\nIf you are on a public computer, Chromebook, or any device without the app installed, you can access your iCloud control dashboard by visiting **[iCloud.com](https://www.icloud.com/)**. From there, you can view your Photos, Mail, Notes, Drive, Reminders, and locate lost devices using \"Find My.\"",
